        "market_heading": "New York 3D architectural rendering for luxury projects",
        "market_text": "<p>New York is where Bella's luxury rendering work starts. We provide the luxury architectural rendering New York developers, architects and brokerages need for the building types that define the city's high end: Manhattan condo towers and their entry sequences, full-floor residences and penthouses, amenity floors with pools, lounges and fitness studios, roof terraces, and townhouse and brownstone projects where an interior renovation has to be seen before anyone will commit.</p><p>New York developers use these images to pre-sell residences from plans, to clarify design intent for investors and lenders, and to create marketing materials for a sales gallery, a broker open or a launch campaign long before construction begins. Whether the project is a tower in Midtown Manhattan or a boutique condo in Brooklyn, a 3D artist models it from your architectural plans, matches every finish to your specification and lights it to sell. Explore <a href=\"/pages/3d-interior-rendering-services\">luxury interior rendering</a> and <a href=\"/pages/3d-exterior-rendering-services\">luxury exterior rendering</a>, compare every service on our <a href=\"/pages/3d-rendering-services\">3D rendering services</a> hub, or order from the <a href=\"/products/3d-rendering-service-for-architectural-visualization\">3D rendering page</a>.</p>",
        "local_heading": "What separates luxury rendering from a standard render",
        "local_text": "<p>Luxury buyers judge quality in the details: whether marble veining runs true across a waterfall island, whether late-afternoon light falls believably across oak floors, whether a lobby feels like somewhere you would want to come home to. A luxury render gets those details right because a human 3D artist builds them, with physically accurate materials, realistic lighting, styling chosen for the buyer and camera angles composed like an architectural photographer's. The result is aesthetic appeal that stays true to the plans.</p><p>There is no luxury surcharge. A penthouse great room is an interior render and a townhouse at dusk is an exterior render, priced by render type and size rather than by the cost of the finishes. A high-rise tower and other complex projects beyond the standard size limits are quoted before you commit, and revisions are included with every render.</p>",
