    "faq": {
      "type": "bella-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is luxury 3D rendering?",
            "answer": "Luxury 3D rendering is photorealistic architectural visualization for high-end residential and commercial projects. A 3D artist models the building from architectural drawings, then applies physically accurate materials, realistic lighting, designer styling and composed camera angles, so penthouses, condo towers, custom homes and amenity spaces look the way they will when finished. Developers, architects and brokerages use luxury renders to market and pre-sell architectural projects before construction is complete."
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much does luxury 3D rendering cost?",
            "answer": "At Bella, luxury renders start at {price:3d-rendering} per finished image for a residential interior. Commercial interiors such as lobbies and amenity spaces, exteriors, streetscapes, aerials and multi-building views are priced per view in the table above, and there is no luxury surcharge. Across the market, 3D rendering prices range from a few hundred to several thousand dollars per image depending on project complexity; animated walkthroughs cost more than stills, and some studios bill extra revision rounds. Bella includes revisions, and volume discounts of up to 20% apply automatically."
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much do architects charge for renderings?",
            "answer": "Architects either produce renderings in-house as part of their design fees or commission an outside rendering studio, which usually charges per image. Bella works directly with architects and architectural firms on residential projects and commercial projects, from {price:3d-rendering} per image."
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does a luxury render take?",
            "answer": "Typically one to two weeks from plans to final renderings, depending on scope and project complexity. Interiors are usually faster than multi-building exteriors. We confirm timing as soon as you send your drawings."
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you offer 3D architectural rendering in New York?",
            "answer": "Yes. New York is Bella's lead luxury market: Manhattan condo towers, penthouses, amenity floors, townhouses and brownstone renovations, anywhere in the five boroughs. We work from your architectural drawings online, so New York developers and architects don't need a studio with a New York office. Drafts, revisions and final delivery all happen remotely."
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does a luxury condominium look like in a render?",
            "answer": "A luxury condo rendering shows the finished residence at its best: generous ceiling heights, floor-to-ceiling windows, stone and timber finishes, designer furniture and warm, realistic lighting, plus the amenities that come with the building. It lets buyers see the specification they are paying for before construction is complete."
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are the different types of architectural renderings?",
            "answer": "The main types are interior renderings, exterior renderings, aerial and streetscape views and 3D site plans, delivered as still images, architectural animation or virtual reality tours. Bella delivers still interior, exterior, streetscape, aerial and multi-building renders for residential and commercial projects."
          }
        },
        "q8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is architectural visualization?",
            "answer": "Architectural visualization is the practice of showing an unbuilt building visually, using 3D rendering to turn architectural drawings into images that clarify design intent for clients, buyers, investors and planning boards. High-end architectural visualization adds the material accuracy, lighting and styling of a luxury marketing campaign, and helps explain complex ideas to people who don't read plans."
          }
        },
        "q9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can ChatGPT do architectural renderings?",
            "answer": "ChatGPT and other AI image tools can generate a picture of a building, but they don't build from your dimensioned plans, so proportions, windows and rooflines drift from the real design. They are useful for early mood boards. For luxury marketing that buyers, lenders and boards rely on, a 3D artist working from your drawings is still the standard."
          }
        },
        "q10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the best rendering software for architecture?",
            "answer": "Studios commonly model in 3ds Max, SketchUp or Revit, render with physically based engines such as V-Ray or Corona, and finish in Photoshop. The software matters less than the artist using it, and you don't need any of it to order: send your drawings and our 3D team does the modelling."
          }
        },
        "q11": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How can I get a luxury house rendering?",
            "answer": "Order an interior or exterior render, then upload floor plans, elevations and finish selections after checkout. A Bella 3D artist models your home from the plans and renders it. Luxury home rendering starts at {price:3d-rendering} per image, and custom home exteriors up to 6,000 sq ft are priced as single-building exterior renders."
          }
        },
        "q12": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you render a luxury interior renovation?",
            "answer": "Yes. Send the existing plans and the proposed design, and we render the renovated space so owners, buyers and boards can see the result before work starts. If you only have photos of the existing room, <a href=\"/products/virtual-renovation-service\">virtual renovation</a> is a faster way to show the new look."
          }
        },
        "q13": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who uses luxury 3D rendering?",
            "answer": "Real estate developers and property developers pre-selling condos and towers, custom home builders, architects and architectural firms presenting to clients, interior designers, construction companies and luxury brokerages marketing new development. Bella's clients include Concord Pacific, Highland Homes and Brown Harris Stevens."
          }
        },
        "q14": {
          "type": "qa",
